.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt NQSELFTEST 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqselftest
.Nd known answers for every algorithm family
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqselftest void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqselftest
runs fixed inputs through the functions of every algorithm family
and compares what they produce with answers built into the library, the kind of self-test a cryptographic module runs before it is
used (FIPS 140-3, which takes its requirements from ISO/IEC 19790:2012,
section 7.10):
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
SHA-224 to SHA-512/256, SHA3-224 to SHA3-512, SHAKE128 and SHAKE256 of
.Dq abc ;
.It
KangarooTwelve and its 256-bit form of
.Dq abc ,
and of 9,000 bytes with the customization string
.Ql noqtis
(a tree of two chunks);
.It
HMAC-SHA-256 and HMAC-SHA-512 (RFC 4231, test case 2);
.It
ML-KEM-512, -768 and -1024: a key pair and an encapsulation from fixed
seeds, and the decapsulation;
.It
ML-DSA-44, -65 and -87: a key pair from a fixed seed, the deterministic
signature of a fixed message and its verification;
.It
SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f and SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128f: a key pair from a fixed seed;
.It
HQC-128: a key pair, an encapsulation and the decapsulation;
.It
Ed25519 and ML-DSA-44+Ed25519: a key pair, a deterministic signature and
its verification;
.It
BLAKE2b-512 of
.Dq abc
(RFC 7693, appendix A);
.It
HKDF-SHA-256 (RFC 5869, test case A.1): the extract and the expand;
.It
PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 (RFC 7914, section 11, one iteration);
.It
Argon2id (RFC 9106, section 5.3: 32 KiB, 3 passes, 4 lanes);
.It
AES-256-GCM (the GCM specification, test case 14) and ChaCha20-Poly1305
(RFC 8439, section 2.8.2): sealing, opening, and opening with a changed
tag, which must fail;
.It
the ChaCha20 stream (RFC 8439, appendix A.2, test vector 1);
.It
AES-SIV (RFC 5297, appendix A.1) and AES-256-GCM-SIV (RFC 8452,
appendix C.2): sealing, opening, and opening a changed ciphertext, which
must fail;
.It
X25519 (RFC 7748, section 5.2, the first vector).
.El
.Pp
That is 17 tests; each of the last ten runs the inputs of the published
vector named, so its stored answer is also the SHA-256 of the return
codes and the published outputs.
Each family's keys, ciphertexts, signatures, secrets and return codes
are hashed with SHA-256; a decapsulation or verification that disagrees
changes the hash.
The masked decapsulations and signers run as in normal use, so the
self-test needs the random source: without one (a freestanding build
with no
.Xr nqsetrng 3 )
it returns
.Er NQEKAT .
The freestanding build has no AES-GCM, ChaCha20, AES-SIV, AES-GCM-SIV
or X25519, and leaves their six tests out; it runs the Argon2id test
only once
.Xr nqsetal 3
has given it an allocator.
It takes about a tenth of a second.
Its buffers are one static block of about 44 KB, wiped after each test,
held under a lock; only Argon2id allocates, 32 KiB through the
.Xr nqsetal 3
hook.
It may be called from several threads at once; one test runs at a
time and the others wait.
The lock is a spin lock, held for one test at a time (well under a
second): a waiting thread spins, using its processor, until the lock is
free.
It is not re-entrant: a random source set with
.Xr nqsetrng 3 ,
which the self-test calls while it holds the lock, must not call
.Fn nqselftest ,
or the call never returns.
The progress and stop hooks
.Pq Xr nqsetprog 3 , Xr nqsetstop 3
are not called during the self-test.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
when every answer matches;
.Dv NQEKAT
when one does not.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if (nqselftest() != NQOK) {
  fputs("noqtis: self-test failed, not used\en", stderr);
  exit(1);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-selftest 1 ,
.Xr nqerr 3 ,
.Xr nqsetal 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T FIPS 140-3: Security Requirements for Cryptographic Modules
.%Q NIST
.%D March 22, 2019
.Re
.Rs
